From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Subject: [PATCH] mm: default to order-zero reporting at a 100ms cadence

Setting prdev->order to zero does not select order-zero reporting: the
registration code treats zero as an unspecified driver preference and
falls back to pageblock_order. Set the reporting core's default instead.
The existing page_reporting.page_reporting_order parameter still overrides
this, including when an operator prefers order 9 to reduce host THP splits.

Use a 100ms reporting delay. Reporting remains event-driven and only runs
when a VMM negotiates VIRTIO_BALLOON_F_REPORTING. It reports free pages;
unlike balloon inflation, it does not reduce guest MemTotal or evict cache.

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
diff --git a/mm/page_reporting.c b/mm/page_reporting.c
--- a/mm/page_reporting.c
+++ b/mm/page_reporting.c
@@ -11,8 +11,8 @@
 #include "page_reporting.h"
 #include "internal.h"
 
-/* Initialize to an unsupported value */
-unsigned int page_reporting_order = -1;
+/* MicroVM default: report even fragmented single free pages. */
+unsigned int page_reporting_order = 0;
 
 static int page_order_update_notify(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
 {
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
  */
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(page_reporting_order);
 
-#define PAGE_REPORTING_DELAY	(2 * HZ)
+#define PAGE_REPORTING_DELAY	msecs_to_jiffies(100)
 static struct page_reporting_dev_info __rcu *pr_dev_info __read_mostly;
 
 enum {
@@ -339,8 +339,8 @@
 err_out:
 	/*
 	 * If the state has reverted back to requested then there may be
-	 * additional pages to be processed. We will defer for 2s to allow
-	 * more pages to accumulate.
+	 * additional pages to be processed. Defer for PAGE_REPORTING_DELAY
+	 * to allow more pages to accumulate.
 	 */
 	state = atomic_cmpxchg(&prdev->state, state, PAGE_REPORTING_IDLE);
 	if (state == PAGE_REPORTING_REQUESTED)
